entries.description:
> **Warning:** This function is broken (at least in arma3
) as it has a typo, displaying an error on each use!  (typo **line 63**, `[centrum]` instead of `[_centrum]`).
This function gets objects (but centre object) positions and direction relative to the choosen object and copies the result to the clipboard via copyToClipboard.

Result is to format:

```sqf
[
	// 11 elements for one object
	_nameOfObject, _objectClass, _objectToGet, _computedAngle, _distance, _newDir, _vectorUp, _vectorDir, _animation, _elevASL, _elev,
	_nameOfObject, _objectClass, _objectToGet, _computedAngle, _distance, _newDir, _vectorUp, _vectorDir, _animation, _elevASL, _elev,
	// ...
]
```

> **Warning:** Please note that the clipboard result is a one-level array, meaning that all parameters are defined one after the other!

This function sets objects positions and direction relative to the chosen object.

> **Warning:** Same as its GET counterpart (at least in arma3
), this function does not work as intended as it does not set objects' direction properly. All objects will be created with a zero azimuth.

